Actually, I just realised something - that patch causes overlap with
eating deep fried tins of said monsters, such that you'll get two
"slippery" messages when eating it. The solution, of course, is to make
the effect exclusive to their (mangled) corpses (which is what you
intended in the first place, is it not?)

~~begin patch
diff -Nurb nethack-3.4.3-original/src/eat.c nethack-3.4.3/src/eat.c
--- nethack-3.4.3-original/src/eat.c    Mon Dec  8 09:39:13 2003
+++ nethack-3.4.3/src/eat.c     Tue Nov 29 22:58:38 2005
@@ -1331,6 +1331,13 @@
                  ? "is delicious" : "tastes terrible");
        }

+       if((amorphous(&mons[mnum]) || slithy(&mons[mnum]) ||
+               &mons[mnum].mlet == S_BLOB) && &mons[mnum].mlet !=
S_MIMIC) {
+           pline("Eating this corpse makes your %s %s slippery.",
+               makeplural(body_part(FINGER)), Glib ? "even more" :
"very");
+           incr_itimeout(&Glib, rnd(15));
+       }
+
        return(retcode);
 }

 ~end patch



